@startuml heap-where-allocations-moved
' ============================================================================
' MEASURED heap profile of the cold-store codec conversion.
' Instruments: valgrind massif (--time-unit=B) and valgrind DHAT, 2026-07-29.
' Raw data: /tmp/sd_massif/*.out, /tmp/sd_dhat/summary.*.txt
'   RED  #C62828 native stack (uncounted by DHAT — that is the point)
'   BLUE #1565C0 heap
'   GREEN #2E7D32 the arena that replaced per-call allocation
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4

title <b>Where the allocations moved</b>  —  cold-store codec, MEASURED\nmassif + DHAT, release, one arm per process, pinned cores

package "**A.  Production shape** (depth 2 = 95.43 % of measured produces), 20,000 encodes" as A #E3F2FD {
  rectangle "**derived** `bincode::serialize`\ntotal **12,828,259 B** in **20,022** blocks\n= **1.001 blocks / call**\npeak **6,187 B** in 15 blocks\nheap **writes** 12.83 MB" as A1 #FFCDD2
  rectangle "**machine** `bincode_encoder::encode`\ntotal **12,834,467 B** in **20,026** blocks\n= **1.001 blocks / call**\npeak **12,395 B** in 19 blocks\nheap **writes** 41.65 MB" as A2 #BBDEFB
  rectangle "**reused** `bincode_encoder::with_encoded`\ntotal **14,466 B** in **26** blocks\n= **0.0013 blocks / call**\npeak **12,394 B** in 19 blocks\nheap **writes** 28.83 MB" as A3 #A5D6A7

  A1 -[#455A64,thickness=2]right-> A2 : **+6,208 B total** (the two thread-local\narenas, allocated **once**);\npeak **2.00<latex>\times</latex>** because the arenas are **retained**
  A2 -[#2E7D32,thickness=2]right-> A3 : **770<latex>\times</latex> fewer blocks**, **887<latex>\times</latex> fewer bytes\nwhen the caller does not need ownership
}

package "**B.  Deep shape** (a 4,096-deep `Par`)" as B #E3F2FD {
  rectangle "**encoder working set**, above the live term:\n**786,432 B**\n= op stack **524,288 B** (16,384 <latex>\times</latex> 32 B `Op`)\n+ output buffer **262,144 B** (holds 148,546 B)\n⇒ **64 B / level** of op stack, <latex>2.00</latex> entries/level" as B1 #90CAF9
  rectangle "**decoder transient working set**:\n**1,248,192 B**, reproduced **to the byte** on\nevery one of the observed decodes\n⇒ **304.7 B / level** of heap value stacks" as B2 #64B5F6
  rectangle "the 4,096-deep term itself:\n**3,080,192 B** live, in 8,193 blocks\n(identical whether **built** or **decoded**)" as B3 #E1BEE7
  B1 -[#1565C0]-> B3
  B2 -[#1565C0]-> B3
}

package "**C.  The migration, per nesting level**" as C #FFF8E1 {
  rectangle "**cold-store WRITER**\nnative <latex>329 \rightarrow 0</latex> B/level  (release)\nheap   <latex>0 \rightarrow 64</latex> B/level\n<b>ratio 5.1<latex>\times</latex> cheaper</b>, and the region is now growable" as C1 #FFE082
  rectangle "**cold-store READER**\nnative <latex>12{,}894 \rightarrow 0</latex> B/level  (release)\nheap   <latex>0 \rightarrow 304.7</latex> B/level\n<b>ratio 42.3<latex>\times</latex> cheaper</b>, and the region is now growable" as C2 #FFE082
}

A -[hidden]-> B
B -[hidden]-> C

note bottom of C #FFF3E0
  ★ **This is the whole trade, in one sentence.** The conversion does not remove the
  <latex>\Theta(d)</latex> state — a depth-<latex>d</latex> traversal must remember <latex>d</latex>
  things. It **relocates** that state from a **fixed 2 MiB region whose exhaustion is a SIGSEGV**
  to a **growable region whose exhaustion is an `Err`** — and, on these two codecs, it happens to
  need 5<latex>\times</latex> to 42<latex>\times</latex> fewer bytes per level as well, because a
  hand-written work item carries only what the resumption needs while a compiler-laid-out stack
  frame carries every live local of a 40-arm `match`.
end note

note right of A #FFEBEE
  ⚠ **The cost, stated plainly.** The machine performs
  **3.25<latex>\times</latex> more heap writes** than the derive on the
  production shape (41.65 MB vs 12.83 MB over 20,000 encodes).
  Those writes were previously native-stack traffic, which DHAT
  does not count — so this is a *relocation made visible*, not new
  work invented. The peak heap **doubles** (6,187 → 12,395 B)
  because the arenas are deliberately retained.
end note

@enduml
